### Combat Flow
Implementation requirements:

1. Attack Resolution
   ```typescript
   const resolveAttack = (attacker: Battalion, target: Battalion) => {
     const damage = calculateDamage(attacker, target);
     applyDamage(target, damage);
     updateCombatState(attacker, target);
   };
   ```
   - Calculate and apply damage
   - Update unit states
   - Trigger effects

2. State Updates
   ```typescript
   const updateCombatState = (attacker: Battalion, target: Battalion) => {
     updateAttackerState(attacker);
     updateTargetState(target);
     notifyCombatEffects(attacker, target);
   };
   ```
   - Update both units
   - Trigger animations
   - Update UI

3. Death Handling
   ```typescript
   const handleUnitDeath = (battalion: Battalion) => {
     if (battalion.totalHealth <= 0) {
       triggerDestructionEffects(battalion);
       removeBattalion(battalion);
     }
   };
   ```
   - Check health status
   - Trigger effects
   - Clean up resources

### Combat Optimization
Implementation requirements:

1. Calculation Caching
   ```typescript
   const combatCache = new Map<string, CombatValues>();
   
   const getCachedValues = (battalion: Battalion) => {
     const key = getCacheKey(battalion);
     if (!combatCache.has(key)) {
       combatCache.set(key, calculateCombatValues(battalion));
     }
     return combatCache.get(key);
   };
   ```
   - Cache common calculations
   - Update on state changes
   - Clear on battle end

2. Batch Processing
   ```typescript
   const batchCombatUpdates = (updates: CombatUpdate[]) => {
     const batch = new CombatBatch(updates);
     batch.process();
     batch.applyEffects();
     batch.notify();
   };
   ```
   - Group similar updates
   - Process in order
   - Apply effects once

Remember: Combat implementation must maintain system integrity and follow core mechanics while ensuring optimal performance. 